<!-- =========================
     WHAT IS ON PAGE SEO
========================= -->

<section class="intro">

    <div class="container">

        <div class="section-title">

            <h2>
                What is <span>On-Page SEO?</span>
            </h2>

            <p>
                Understanding the basics of webpage optimization
            </p>

        </div>


        <div class="intro-box">

            <p>
                On-Page SEO refers to optimizing the content and
                elements present on a webpage so that users can
                understand the content easily and search engines
                can better interpret the page.
            </p>

            <p>
                It includes different elements such as keywords,
                title tags, meta descriptions, headings, URLs,
                internal links, images and content structure.
            </p>

            <p>
                Good On-Page SEO focuses on creating useful,
                relevant and well-organized content that addresses
                the user's search intent.
            </p>

            <p>
                As an SEO Intern, I am learning and practicing these
                elements to understand how webpage optimization works
                in real projects.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
     SEO ELEMENTS
========================= -->

<section id="seo-elements">

    <div class="container">

        <div class="section-title">

