</section>


<!-- =========================
     DETAILED SEO
========================= -->

<section class="details">

    <div class="container">

        <div class="section-title">

            <h2>
                On-Page SEO <span>In Detail</span>
            </h2>

            <p>
                Simple examples of important SEO elements
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- KEYWORD RESEARCH -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                1. Keyword Research
            </h3>

            <p>
                Keyword research helps identify the words and phrases
                people use when searching for information, products
                or services.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                If your page is about online medicine delivery in Jaipur,
                a relevant keyword could be
                <strong>"online medicine delivery Jaipur"</strong>.

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- TITLE TAG -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                2. Title Tag
            </h3>

            <p>
                The title tag describes the main topic of a webpage.
                It should be clear, relevant and useful to the user.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                Online Medicine Delivery in Jaipur | Direct Dawai

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- META DESCRIPTION -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                3. Meta Description
            </h3>

            <p>
                A meta description provides a short summary of the
                webpage content.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                Order medicines online in Jaipur with convenient
                delivery and explore a wide range of healthcare products.

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- HEADINGS -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                4. Heading Structure
            </h3>

            <p>
                Headings help divide webpage content into meaningful
                sections and make the content easier to scan.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong><br><br>

                H1 → Online Medicine Delivery in Jaipur<br>

                H2 → Why Choose Online Medicine Delivery?<br>

                H2 → How to Order Medicines Online?<br>

                H3 → Steps to Place an Order

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- URL -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                5. SEO-Friendly URL
            </h3>

            <p>
                A descriptive URL helps communicate the topic of
                the webpage in a simple and readable format.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong><br><br>

                Good:
                example.com/online-medicine-delivery-jaipur

                <br><br>

                Avoid:
                example.com/page?id=12345

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- INTERNAL LINKING -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                6. Internal Linking
            </h3>

            <p>
                Internal links connect one page of a website to
                another relevant page on the same website.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                An SEO article about keyword research can link to
                another relevant page about On-Page SEO.

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- IMAGE SEO -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                7. Image SEO
            </h3>

            <p>
                Images can be optimized by using descriptive file
                names, suitable image formats and meaningful alt text.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong><br><br>

                File name:
                online-medicine-delivery-jaipur.jpg

                <br><br>

                Alt text:
                Online medicine delivery service in Jaipur

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- CONTENT -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                8. Content Optimization
            </h3>

            <p>
                Content should be useful, relevant, readable and
                organized around the user's needs.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                Use relevant keywords naturally while keeping the
                content useful and easy to read.

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- SEARCH INTENT -->

        <div class="detail-box">

            <h3>
                9. Search Intent
            </h3>

            <p>
                Search intent refers to the reason behind a user's
                search query.
            </p>

            <div class="example">

                <strong>Example:</strong>

                A person searching "what is On-Page SEO" is likely
                looking for information, while someone searching
                "SEO course near me" may be looking for a service
                or course.

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>


